From: Nicolas Villar <15879262+nvillar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:44:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: predictive Back previews only tasks of the gestured
 panel

BackNavigationController.startBackNavigation picks the task Back would reveal (back-to-home / cross-task check) by
walking the whole window hierarchy below the current task. The focused panel's group is on top, so from a panel task
that walk reached the other panel's task (or, from the lower panel, the spanned home). Back from panel 0 with panel 0
focused (focus moves there on the touch down of the gesture) prepared a TYPE_CROSS_TASK animation that closed the
panel 0 task and "opened" the already visible panel 1 task: Shell scaled and moved the other panel's task with the
gesture, and WindowState.canReceiveTouchInput paused touch on it for as long as the animation was composed (input
window NO_INPUT_CHANNEL | NOT_TOUCHABLE, taps fell through to the spanned home behind it; ledger F22). Neither of those
tasks is what Back shows: Back finishes or minimizes the panel task and the panel then shows its next task or home.

For a task in a panel task area the candidates are now only the tasks of that panel that are not force hidden (a task
minimized by Home or by Back stays hidden when the current task goes away). With another task in the panel the cross
task preview is the platform's, inside the panel. With none, no preview is prepared (TYPE_CALLBACK): Back is still
delivered to the app on commit, and a cancelled gesture prepares no transition and changes nothing. In a single panel
posture (both panel groups cover the same screen) and in the spanned default task area (home, recents and spanned
apps) the platform search applies. The search moves to DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.previousTaskForBack, which returns
the platform result when the policy is not active.

Not built or run on a device yet. Verified by git am -3 after the series and a javac type check of the changed classes
against the gate build's framework and services jars.

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../server/wm/BackNavigationController.java   |  5 ++--
 .../wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java      | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/BackNavigationController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/BackNavigationController.java
index b9be7b960..a0b517bbc 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/BackNavigationController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/BackNavigationController.java
@@ -389,13 +389,14 @@ class BackNavigationController {
                 backType = BackNavigationInfo.TYPE_CALLBACK;
             } else {
                 // Check back-to-home or cross-task
-                prevTask = currentTask.mRootWindowContainer.getTask(t -> {
+                // Duo two panel policy: a panel task only previews the tasks of its own panel.
+                prevTask = DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.previousTaskForBack(currentTask, t -> {
                     if (t.showToCurrentUser() && !t.mChildren.isEmpty()) {
                         final ActivityRecord ar = t.getTopNonFinishingActivity();
                         return ar != null && ar.showToCurrentUser();
                     }
                     return false;
-                }, currentTask, false /*includeBoundary*/, true /*traverseTopToBottom*/);
+                });
                 final ActivityRecord tmpPre = prevTask != null
                         ? prevTask.getTopNonFinishingActivity() : null;
                 if (tmpPre != null) {
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java
index db98daca4..7c9d85bd8 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider.java
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ import com.android.server.wm.DisplayAreaPolicyBuilder.HierarchyBuilder;
 
 import java.util.ArrayList;
 import java.util.function.Consumer;
+import java.util.function.Predicate;
 import java.util.List;
 
 /**
@@ -235,6 +236,29 @@ public class DuoDisplayAreaPolicyProvider implements DisplayAreaPolicy.Provider
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * The task predictive Back would reveal below {@code current} (BackNavigationController, back-to-home or cross-task
+     * check). The platform walks the whole hierarchy, which from a panel task reaches the other panel's task (the
+     * focused panel's group is on top) or the spanned home: the preview then animated and paused for touch the task on
+     * the other panel, and Back is not going to show either of them. For a panel task only the tasks of its own panel
+     * are candidates, and only ones that are not force hidden (minimized by the policy, or hidden by an organizer: they
+     * stay hidden when the current task goes away). No candidate means no preview: Back is still delivered to the app.
+     * In a single panel posture both panel groups cover the same screen and the platform search applies.
+     */
+    @Nullable
+    static Task previousTaskForBack(Task current, Predicate<Task> candidate) {
+        final TaskDisplayArea tda = sActive ? current.getDisplayArea() : null;
+        if (tda == null || !(tda.getRootDisplayArea() instanceof PanelGroup) || tda.getBounds().isEmpty()
+                || tda.getBounds().equals(tda.mDisplayContent.getBounds())) {
+            return current.mRootWindowContainer.getTask(candidate, current, false /* includeBoundary */,
+                    true /* traverseTopToBottom */);
+        }
+        return tda.getTask(t -> {
+            final Task root = t.getRootTask();
+            return (root == null || !root.isForceHidden()) && candidate.test(t);
+        }, current, false /* includeBoundary */, true /* traverseTopToBottom */);
+    }
+
     /**
      * The panel a launch should go to, from where the user tapped. A launcher passes the on-screen rectangle of the
      * tapped icon as the intent's source bounds; the panel containing it gets the new task, so an icon on the left
